<title>AUSTRALIA: ICI says foreign company could make bid.</title>
<headline>ICI says foreign company could make bid.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemicals group ICI Australia Ltd said on Sunday it was possible a foreign company could make a bid for it following plans by its British parent Imperial Chemical Industries Plc to sell its 62.4 percent sometime in July.</p>
<p>ICI Australia managing director Warren Haynes said on Sunday he was expecting foreign ownership of the company would be about 50 percent of the 62.4 percent stake ICI Plc is putting on the market if a competitor does not buy the whole company.</p>
</text>
